{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>For every matter of trespass.</b> Midrash — ״על כל דבר פשע״: in gematria this is אהרן. The trespass (פשע) that he trespassed over the ox — on account of that matter. ״על חמור״ — on account of the mixed multitude that they made in Egypt, who are called חמור, as it is written: ״אשר בשר חמורים בשרם״. ״על שה״ — on account that they caused Israel to sin, who are called שה, ״שה פזורה ישראל״. ״על שלמה״ — on account of the idol, and שי\"ן and צד\"י are interchangeable. ״על כל אבדה״ — also idolatry, as it is said: ״אבד תאבדון״. ״אשר יאמר כי הוא זה״ — this is what they said: ״אלה אלהיך ישראל״. ״עד האלהים״ — this is Moses, as it is written: ״ראה נתתיך אלהים לפרעה״. Let the matter of both of them come — that of the Holy One, blessed be He, and that of Aaron. ״אשר ירשיעון״ — this is Moses. ״ישלם שנים״ — the two sons of Aaron who died."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The text preserves midrashic readings that string together phrases from the verse and assign each a historical referent (Aaron, the mixed multitude, the golden calf, Moses, Nadav and Avihu). The phrase אשר בשר חמורים בשרם is cited as written; שה פזורה ישראל likely echoes Ezekiel 34 and Lamentations. The interchange of שי\"ן and צד\"י is a standard scribal/phonetic substitution."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:57.265766625Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}